---
import DefaultLayout from '@layouts/DefaultLayout.astro'
import PageHeader from '@components/PageHeader.astro'
import ContentMedia from '@components/ContentMedia.astro'
import { Accordion, AccordionItem } from 'accessible-astro-components'
---

<DefaultLayout
  title="About"
  description="Learn about our movement, mission, and the people working for change"
>
  <PageHeader>
    <h1>About This Template</h1>
    <p>Why we built it, how it saves you time, and what makes it different</p>
  </PageHeader>

  <section class="container">
    <ContentMedia imgSrc="/images/placeholder-movement.jpg" reverseImg={false}>
      <h2>Built from Real Experience</h2>
      <p>
        This template came from building dozens of campaign and nonprofit websites. We kept seeing the same 
        problems: broken accessibility, slow deployment, security vulnerabilities, and sites that crashed 
        during important moments.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>What's different:</strong> This template includes solutions to those common problems baked in. 
        Accessibility testing, performance optimization, security headers, and stress-tested deployment 
        patterns so you don't have to figure them out under pressure.
      </p>
    </ContentMedia>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <ContentMedia imgSrc="/images/placeholder-organizing.jpg" reverseImg={true}>
      <h2>How It Saves You Time</h2>
      <p>
        Instead of spending weeks setting up infrastructure, you can focus on content and strategy. 
        The template handles the technical complexity so you can concentrate on what matters: 
        reaching people and building support.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Skip accessibility testing:</strong> Components are pre-tested with screen readers and keyboards</li>
        <li><strong>Environment-based config:</strong> Change branding and features without touching code</li>
        <li><strong>Deploy anywhere:</strong> Works with Netlify, Vercel, or any static hosting service</li>
        <li><strong>Handle traffic spikes:</strong> Static generation means no server crashes during viral moments</li>
      </ul>
    </ContentMedia>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-section">
      <Accordion>
        <AccordionItem header="How do I customize the template?">
          <p>
            <strong>Environment variables:</strong> Most customization happens through .env files—change 
            site name, colors, feature toggles, and contact information without touching code.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Content:</strong> Add stories, events, and updates by creating Markdown files in the 
            content directories. The schema is already configured and type-safe.
          </p>
        </AccordionItem>
        
        <AccordionItem header="What's included out of the box?">
          <p>
            <strong>Content collections:</strong> Stories, events, and updates with proper schemas and 
            pagination. <strong>Accessibility:</strong> WCAG AA compliance, keyboard navigation, screen reader support.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Performance:</strong> Static generation, image optimization, and tree-shaking. 
            <strong>Security:</strong> CSP headers, HTTPS enforcement, and privacy-focused defaults.
          </p>
        </AccordionItem>
        
        <AccordionItem header="How do I deploy it?">
          <p>
            <strong>Netlify (recommended):</strong> Connect your repo, set environment variables, 
            and deploy. Staging and production branches are pre-configured.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Other hosts:</strong> Works with Vercel, GitHub Pages, or any static hosting. 
            Build command is `npm run build` and output directory is `dist/`.
          </p>
        </AccordionItem>
        
        <AccordionItem header="Do I need technical expertise?">
          <p>
            <strong>For setup:</strong> Basic familiarity with Git and environment variables. 
            The documentation includes step-by-step instructions for common tasks.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>For content:</strong> Content editors can add stories and events using Markdown. 
            No coding required once the initial setup is complete.
          </p>
        </AccordionItem>
      </Accordion>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <div class="values-grid">
      <div class="value-card">
        <h3>Developer-Friendly</h3>
        <p>Clear documentation, TypeScript support, and patterns that experienced developers recognize. No mysterious magic or hidden complexity.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card">
        <h3>User-Tested</h3>
        <p>Built from real campaign and nonprofit website experience. Every feature addresses problems we've actually encountered in production.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card">
        <h3>Performance-First</h3>
        <p>Optimized for speed and reliability under pressure. Your site works when traffic spikes during viral moments or breaking news.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card">
        <h3>Accessible by Default</h3>
        <p>WCAG compliance, keyboard navigation, and screen reader support built-in. Skip the accessibility audit—it's already handled.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</DefaultLayout>

<style lang="scss">
  .section-title {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin: 4rem 0 2rem;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--heading-color);
  }

  .faq-section {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto 4rem;
  }

  .values-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
    margin: 3rem 0;
  }

  .value-card {
    padding: 2rem;
    background: var(--background-alt);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    border: 2px solid var(--border-color);
    text-align: center;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
    
    &:hover {
      transform: translateY(-4px);
      box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    }
    
    h3 {
      color: var(--primary-color, #2563eb);
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }
    
    p {
      color: var(--text-color);
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin: 0;
    }
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    
    li {
      margin: 0.5rem 0;
      color: var(--text-color);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
  }
</style>